-- Claim check, batch 2 (3 Nov 2026). Param's rule: no unverified claims from artists.
-- Sources and the dropped claims are in research/claims/out2.json. Old bios kept below so each change can be undone.
-- Two judgement calls: Suchi's venue list came only from an artist-supplied RA bio, so it is out. F1 Singapore for Indo Warehouse rested on a search snippet, so it is out.
-- OLD indo-warehouse: Indo Warehouse is a record label and experiential series founded by Kunal Merchant and Kahani (Armaan Gupta) that showcases the beauty of South Asian culture, music, and rhythm within the global language of electronic music. They coined the genre "Indo House", fusing deep techno beats with South Asian classical influences. In just three years, they moved from intimate New York clubs to sold-out international venues across Europe, Asia, and the Middle East. Their performances feature up to 25 performers including musicians, vocalists, and dancers. Historic Coachella 2025 debut as first South Asian electronic collective. Performed at Hï Ibiza, F1 Singapore, DGTL, Magnetic Fields, and Lollapalooza.
-- OLD nikki-nair: (press-kit text with Mixmag top 25, DJ Mag 12 artists, Knoxville, most booked, personal hero claims)
-- OLD prismer: (included London 2010, Denham Audio, Bass Camp, Boiler Room Delhi NCR, Apple Music, marginalised communities)
-- OLD stain: Stain is Sourodeep Guha, a DJ and producer based in Delhi. He plays bass-heavy club music rooted in sound system culture, with dub and Afrobeat influences. He co-founded the Delhi bass collective Sub-Z and has had support from Om Unit, dBridge, Zed Bias and Mala.
-- OLD suchi: (press-kit text with Indian heritage, Pitchfork/Vogue/Rolling Stone, supporters list, Jon Hopkins tour, Cadavra)
update artists set bio = $b$SUCHI is a DJ and producer who was born in Oslo and raised in London. Her sets draw on house, percussion, bass, breaks and techno. Mixmag listed her among its top 25 artists to watch in 2022. In 2025 she launched her label Ikke Sant, whose first release is the three-track Sub Cut EP. She played Boiler Room India in Bangalore and Hyderabad in 2022.$b$ where slug = 'suchi';
update artists set bio = $b$Nikki Nair is a Tennessee-born, Atlanta-based producer and DJ whose music mixes US Southeast bass with UK and other influences. He launched his label n goes to infinity in February 2022. In 2023 he made the mini-album Set the Roof with Hudson Mohawke, whose music he has followed since 2010. Crack Magazine included him in its Signing Off series on the artists who defined 2023.$b$ where slug = 'nikki-nair';
update artists set bio = $b$Indo Warehouse is a record label and event series founded in 2022 by Kunal Merchant and Kahani (Armaan Gupta). They coined the term Indo House for their mix of South Asian elements with house and techno. Their first party was a 200-person night on New York's Lower East Side in February 2022, and they have since played across Europe, Asia and the Middle East, including Hï Ibiza. In 2025 they were the first South Asian electronic collective to play Coachella, with more than 25 performers on stage in weekend one.$b$ where slug = 'indo-warehouse';
update artists set bio = $b$Prismer is Rohan Kale, a New Delhi producer and DJ whose music runs across techno, jungle, drum and bass, dubstep, breakbeat and house. His early releases came out on Boxout.FM, Reel Long Overdub and Tokyo Hell. He has played alongside DJ Stingray, Pangaea, Ivy Lab and Rider Shafique, and has played Magnetic Fields and Grasslands in Nepal. He was on the bill for The Warehouse Project India in October 2025. He started the Delhi party series Mixed Feelings, which he describes as a safe space.$b$ where slug = 'prismer';
update artists set bio = $b$Stain is Sourodeep Guha, a DJ and producer based in New Delhi. He makes bass music with dub and Afrobeat influences. He is a founding member of the Delhi bass collective Sub-Z. During Zed Bias's India tour he worked with him on the track Delhi Birds.$b$ where slug = 'stain';
